From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:11:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 026/207] server: render DeepSeek-V4.x chat with its own
 encoder and schema prompt

DeepSeek-V4.x releases ship encoding.py, not a Jinja template. A
checkpoint that carries one anyway (flash17 keeps September's file for
older loaders) made every chat prompt render through that stale file
instead of the native encoder the published engine uses, changing
prompt ids, effort defaults and tool rules. The native encoder now
renders DeepSeek-V4.x unless --chat-template names an override.

The native path also covers what the Jinja path did: image parts become
the image token when the server serves images (still refused otherwise),
and a request's response_format schema is shown as the encoder's
"## Response Format" block, as the published engine does by default
(TF_DSV41_SCHEMA_PROMPT=0 turns it off). /tokenize renders the same way.

Host tests run the committed encoding.py goldens, now including the
response_format cases, through HfText; cover the ignored checkpoint
Jinja, the override, served and refused images, json_object, string and
object schemas and the knob.
